To design and implement a website prototype for UC Berkeley using JavaScript, we will use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript to create a modern, responsive landing page. We'll use a JavaScript framework like React to manage the components and state of the application. For styling, we'll use CSS with a preprocessor like Sass for better organization and maintainability. We'll ensure the design is mobile-friendly and accessible.

### Core Components and Functions

1. **App Component**: The main component that will render the entire application.
   - Purpose: Serve as the entry point for the application.

2. **Header Component**: Contains the university's brand elements and navigation.
   - Purpose: Display the logo and navigation links for major sections.

3. **MainContent Component**: Contains the main sections of the website.
   - Purpose: Display sections like admissions, academics, research, etc.

4. **NewsEvents Component**: Displays the news or events section.
   - Purpose: Show the latest news and events related to the university.

5. **Footer Component**: Contains footer information and links.
   - Purpose: Provide additional navigation and contact information.

6. **Responsive Design**: Use CSS media queries to ensure the site is mobile-friendly.
   - Purpose: Adapt the layout for different screen sizes.

7. **Accessibility Features**: Implement ARIA roles and keyboard navigation.
   - Purpose: Ensure the site is accessible to users with disabilities.

### File Structure

1. `index.html`: The main HTML file.
2. `App.js`: The main React component.
3. `Header.js`: The header component.
4. `MainContent.js`: The main content component.
5. `NewsEvents.js`: The news and events component.
6. `Footer.js`: The footer component.
7. `styles.scss`: The main stylesheet.

### Code Implementation

#### index.html

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>UC Berkeley</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div id="root"></div>
    <script src="bundle.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

#### App.js

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import Header from './Header';
import MainContent from './MainContent';
import NewsEvents from './NewsEvents';
import Footer from './Footer';

function App() {
    return (
        <div>
            <Header />
            <MainContent />
            <NewsEvents />
            <Footer />
        </div>
    );
}

export default App;
```

#### Header.js

```javascript
import React from 'react';

function Header() {
    return (
        <header>
            <div className="logo">UC Berkeley</div>
            <nav>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="#admissions">Admissions</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#academics">Academics</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#research">Research</a></li>
                </ul>
            </nav>
        </header>
    );
}

export default Header;
```

#### MainContent.js

```javascript
import React from 'react';

function MainContent() {
    return (
        <main>
            <section id="admissions">
                <h2>Admissions</h2>
                <p>Information about admissions.</p>
            </section>
            <section id="academics">
                <h2>Academics</h2>
                <p>Information about academics.</p>
            </section>
            <section id="research">
                <h2>Research</h2>
                <p>Information about research.</p>
            </section>
        </main>
    );
}

export default MainContent;
```

#### NewsEvents.js

```javascript
import React from 'react';

function NewsEvents() {
    return (
        <section id="news-events">
            <h2>News & Events</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Event 1</li>
                <li>Event 2</li>
                <li>Event 3</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
    );
}

export default NewsEvents;
```

#### Footer.js

```javascript
import React from 'react';

function Footer() {
    return (
        <footer>
            <p>© 2023 UC Berkeley</p>
            <nav>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#privacy">Privacy Policy</a></li>
                </ul>
            </nav>
        </footer>
    );
}

export default Footer;
```

#### styles.scss

```scss
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

header {
    background-color: #003262;
    color: white;
    padding: 10px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
}

nav ul {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
}

main {
    padding: 20px;
}

footer {
    background-color: #f2f2f2;
    padding: 10px;
    text-align: center;
}

@media (max-width: 600px) {
    nav ul {
        flex-direction: column;
    }
}
```

This implementation provides a basic structure for a responsive and accessible website prototype for UC Berkeley. The use of React components allows for modular and reusable code, while the CSS ensures a modern and responsive design.

